ng same\".\n  - **A stale explanation.** Kept sentences still explain the empty close and the second-lane close through a source-branch rule and an empty id list. The code now has neither: the one-row clause (`len(deleted) != 1`) refuses both shapes, and the composer takes a single id and refuses anything else by type. Sitting 005 asked for this to be fixed, carrying REVIEW-A 004's MINOR. TC-205's new sentence (\"one deletion implies one source branch\") now contradicts the sentences after it.\n\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-061 Detail, Title -> before: on a lane claimed with more than one row, the prompt adds every assigned row with its walk state, read off the two-part completion predicate -> after: the prompt is for exactly one assigned work item (its id, title and SpecRef), and an empty, malformed, repeated or multi-item assignment refuses by name before any worker session starts. Every other clause is kept verbatim, AGENTS.md, docs/status.md, the exact reviewed commit and the blocked trailer channel included -> not the same: cardinality narrows and a refusal is added. Ready to bless. It is the spec's LLR-061 target, the refusal arms match the arms map, and it adds no code name.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-061 Method -> before: the two-row prompt-block and `started, not closed` walk arms -> after: an empty, malformed, repeated or list assignment, including an explicit empty one, is refused by name before provider launch with no claim, lock or worktree made; a committed trailer with the spec still open reads built but not done. Every other arm is kept verbatim -> not the same: the verified set changes. Ready to bless:\n  - It answers REVIEW-B 003's and REVIEW-A 004's MINORs on the retired walk vocabulary.\n  - The kept stale-assignment arm still has its code (`stale_terminal_assignment`) and its test.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-144 Detail -> before: the close moves each claimed spec, and a refusal restores every report -> after: the close moves the one spec; a claim of zero items