attestation/gate row surfaces even under keep-nondependent and never has its hold released; a delegated-tier row admits one at a time, exclusive. Exit 0 naming the open-items cards, the kind classification, the ladder and the census are kept -> not the same: the batch arm retires and the stale single-approve sentence is corrected to the code's surface arm. Ready to bless. Two notes, neither a finding:\n  - The keep-nondependent sentence repeats one the cell already states.\n  - \"a row whose approval tier is delegated\" reads as attestation/gate rows, because only rows that await an approval have an approval tier.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-152 Detail -> before: a mixed batch fails toward the bar, and the batch's strictest bar value is forwarded -> after: a lane whose one claimed row is any other kind runs the bar, and that one row's declared value is forwarded. The rest is verbatim -> not the same: the batch arms become one-row arms. Ready to bless. The corrupted character sitting 005 found is gone.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-058 Method -> before: traincar order -> after: work-item order; the named views are kept -> not the same: the ordered unit changes. Ready to bless.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-143 Method -> before: every spine row admits as one batch, and single-approve admits the queued approval batch at the close -> after: the first spine row admits alone and the rest wait; held attestation/gate rows drain and surface at keep-nondependent's close without releasing their hold; autonomous rows dispatch exclusive, one at a time -> not the same: the verified set changes. Ready to bless. It asserts the clause sitting 005 found unverified, and it matches LLR-149.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-154 Method -> before: ahead of a ready spine batch -> after: ahead of a ready spine work item; the red-TC citer and census-grammar arms are kept -> not the same: the unit changes. Ready to bless.\n- [MEANING] TC-205 Method -> before: the batch-shape arm (a two-row close seeded out of order peels un