{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nfor name,kind,ident,field in [\n ('docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml','design','LLR-207','detail'),\n ('docs/test/test-cases.toml','test','TC-205','method'),\n]:\n t=Path(name).read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n b=re.search(rf'\\\\[{kind}\\\\.{ident}\\\\](.*?)(?=\\\\n\\\\[{kind}\\\\.|\\\\Z)',t,re.S).group(1)\n print(ident)\n print(re.search(rf'\"'^{field} = (.*?)(?='\"\\\\n\\\\w+ =|\\\\Z)',b,re.M|re.S).group(1))\n'@ | python -\"","aggregated_output":"LLR-207\r\n\"\"\"tree_identity folds raw NUL-delimited `git ls-tree -r -z` entries after dropping docs/reviews/, docs/log.d/ and docs/iteration/, and returns a 64-hex SHA-256 identity. fold_listing accepts bytes and preserves every path byte so display quoting or decoding cannot merge distinct work trees. A Bar-Green attestation is exactly one column-0 label line, `Bar-Green: tree=<40 hex> work=<40 hex> bar=<review|landing|no-bar> tests=<64 hex|none> <summary>`; its verifier returns fields only when tree and work equal the commit's own tree and first parent and bar is in that set. tests carries none for an empty named test-path set; otherwise it carries the SHA-256 of that set after path separators and leading ./ are normalized, duplicates are removed, and the paths are joined in sorted order. Thus one set in any order or spelling has one value, and a different set has a different value. refresh_attestation admits a refresh subject only with that verified attestation and bar landing or no-bar, so work_tip never peels a review attestation as a refresh; the read-only identity walk still steps through any commit whose non-record identity equals its parent, including an empty review attestation. One producer writes every attestation: it fixes the staged tree before the bar, refuses a red bar or one that leaves the index or worktree off that tree, and restores the index on every failed write; its line joins the message's final trailer block. The attest route refuses before the bar when commit hooks are off, the primary checkout holds the branch, the worktree is dirty (including untracked files), the review-bar declaration is absent or empty, the message carries the label, or the harness floor refuses; it reads the review bar and named tests from the attested lane's own declarations, with no default. A trailer without bar is not read. work_tip peels only a verified refresh at the tip for the reset path; governing_rev is read-only and walks across commits whose non-record identity equals their first parent's, peeling any DISPOSABLE commit it meets to reach one those commits would otherwise hide, and ending at the first commit whose identity differs from its parent's or at its absent-parent and depth bounds - so a branch with no disposable commit under it still walks. TWO commit classes are disposable and the read-only walk peels BOTH: the station's REFRESH, admitted by refresh_attestation, and the machinery's OWN adjudication close, admitted by mechanical_close_attestation against exactly one parent and a no-renames changed-path stream lying wholly under docs/work/. That stream must pair deleted specs from exactly ONE docs/work/active/<branch>/ with additions of the same filenames under docs/work/complete/, and ONLY the move itself may create or destroy: an addition or deletion under docs/work/ that is not one half of a recognised move refuses the whole commit, since peeling it would measure a spec's injection or an archived row's destruction at the parent, where no reviewer saw it. Modifications ride along unrestricted, because a close's inbound relink rewrites other rows in place and only ever modifies. A mechanical close admits exactly one moved row; any other shape declines to peel toward more review. Its subject must equal the writer's composed subject exactly, so a public prefix/suffix with a forged middle is not an attestation. The commit that moved NOTHING is refused by that pairing rather than by a clause of its own: it names no source branch, and its empty id list composes a subject no real close carries. One property admits the two classes and it is not two rules: both are machine-authored end to end, and both move the tree without the lane having changed what it CLAIMS - docs/work/ is deliberately inside the identity because a spec's own claims are what a verdict is about, and the close carries those claims through unchanged. Every arm of both verifications fails toward REVIEW, since declining to peel measures at a later rev and can never ask for LESS - though not always for more: on the empty close the refused commit is identity-preserving, so the walk-through step reaches the same rev the peel would have, and the refusal guards this function's contract rather than any answer the gate gives. The two peels are NOT the same peel: work_tip calls refresh_attestation directly rather than through the shared disposable test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path, which may only ever drop a refresh sitting literally on the tip. governing_identity composes governing_rev and tree_identity for the branch tip or an explicit revision, including a round's reviewed commit and a trailer's carrier; the branch argument is a branch NAME, because the peel verifies a refresh commit against the branch it names and no refresh subject names HEAD. format_scope records a REVIEW session scope as full, narrow or final base..sha; gating_span admits a fresh full scope in either mode, or a final scope only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted; a narrow scope and a retained full scope never admit. logged_rounds joins branch-scoped round files to coordinator session logs by train and ordinal, and each round's review phase is the JOINED LOG's declared phase rather than the one its own filename carries, so a file cannot claim a phase its session did not serve; a joined key whose logs declare more than one review phase yields no round. It retains only a gating span whose base equals the caller's claim base and whose reviewed sha the round file names. round_entries retains only rounds whose reviewed revision governs the identity under judgement and emits phase, ordinal and verdict entries through an injected parser. filing_refusal applies one filing check: the first physical line is exactly the Reviewed full-sha opener (a CR ending is allowed; no leading blank or whitespace is), exactly one canonical VERDICT line, a finding count matching the file, and a change request naming a finding. An unreadable or refused round is an entry with no verdict, so it is the phase's latest word rather than an older verdict being used. tree_already_judged is true only for an entry carrying a verdict and false with no base. declared_phases clamps the configured independent-review count to the available review phases. phases_owed returns declared phases whose latest entry is missing or invalid evidence; a dissent is served. round_count returns the largest per-phase entry count at one governing identity, so a multi-phase review cycle counts once and changed work starts a new count. format_trailer and parse_trailer carry `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>`. branch_trailers verifies each carrier against its governing identity and returns the ordered attestation sequence per tree. Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract.\"\"\"\r\nTC-205\r\n\"\"\"The verdict record's two halves, each driven beside its opposite so neither reads as a rule with one answer. THE IDENTITY, pure over synthetic `git ls-tree -r` entries: a listing and the same listing plus a round file, a log fragment and a session log fold EQUAL, while a changed work blob and a changed docs/work/ spec each fold DIFFERENT - so the exclusion is proven to be an exclusion rather than a fold that ignores everything. THE ENCODING BOUNDARY, driven through git rather than asserted about it: a record path holding a non-ASCII character - the shape git QUOTES, asserted in the fixture so it cannot silently stop reproducing - leaves the identity unmoved, while an accented WORK path moves it; and raw listings with one blob renamed from invalid-UTF-8 path byte 200 to 201 - asserted to COLLIDE under replacement decoding - fold DIFFERENT through tree_identity, so parsing and the ASCII record-prefix boundary occur before any decode. THE TRAILER GRAMMAR: format/parse round-trip; the LAST trailer in a message governs, so a rework commit quoting the round it answers does not have the quotation read as its own attestation; and three malformed shapes - a verdict word outside the enum, a 40-hex tree, a missing round count - each fail to PARSE rather than parse to something. THE NAME PARSE: a round file with and without the relaxed tag, the pre-train flat layout, a session log, and the legacy hand-authored rollup answering None because it names no reviewed sha. THE GATE, on a two-branch git fixture with the trunk checked out: a logged reviewer round naming the current tree clears it with NO rollup present anywhere; the same file with a BUILD session log behind it does not (the implementer-authored round); a SECOND round file committed behind that ONE session log, whose NAME claims the other declared phase, is not a second reviewer - both files are asserted committed and the single log with them, the entries carry the LOG's phase, so at a declared policy of 2 REVIEW-B is still outstanding and the gate refuses by name until a REVIEW-B whose own session log declares it arrives and clears it; TWO session logs at ONE (train, ordinal) declaring DIFFERENT review phases - both asserted committed, with the round file they would otherwise phase asserted still present so the empty answer is the ambiguity rule and not an empty scan - serve NO round at all rather than letting the last log read win, and the gate refuses by name while the single-log arm beside it clears; a round whose tree was reworked away does not, while a log-fragment and scoreboard commit after a round leaves it governing; a CHANGES-REQUESTED round refuses; and a verified Review-Verdict trailer contradicting the rounds refuses by name in its verdict word and in a round count ABOVE the evidence, while a count BELOW it does NOT - both directions driven, because the writer is best-effort and a stamp the evidence outruns is a missed stamp whose refusal parked an approved lane at the very stop the cross-check exists to prevent - and TWO attestations at one governing tree leave the NEWEST governing so a legitimately re-drawn round is not accused of forgery. THE CARRIER IS VERIFIED AND NOT ONLY PARSED, which is what \"the trailer cannot create an approval\" costs: the identical attestation words on a commit that CHANGED the work under them - asserted in the fixture to have really moved the governing identity - are read at neither the tree they NAME nor the tree they rode, beside the record-only carrier of the same words that IS read, so copying a true attestation onto later work buys nothing. THE WRITER IS DRIVEN END TO END, not only the trailer helper: a completed round is run through the loop's own complete_review_round on a repository fixture and the commit it lands is asserted to CARRY the attestation, to name the governing tree, to be read back by the branch reader under the key the cross-check looks up, to leave that governing tree unmoved, and to satisfy the gate - the whole path between a round completing and its attestation landing, which every other trailer case skipped by committing the string itself, and which nothing anywhere reports when it stops writing because absence is the state the cross-check must stand down on. THE RESUME'S OWED SET IS THE EVIDENCE'S ALONE: with both declared phases served at the governing tree and a stale untracked owed-marker still present - the state a run killed between the last reviewer's commit and the round completing leaves - the resume is asserted to queue NOTHING, and beside it a genuine rework with one phase redrawn is asserted to queue that phase and only it. THE PEEL: a genuine Bar-Green refresh commit, verified against its own tree and parent, moves the branch tip's identity and neither reader's answer - the loop still says no round is owed and the gate still merges - which is the one commit class two separately-chosen revs disagreed on; and the same refresh with a coordinator TELEMETRY commit stacked on top of it - a record path, so the fold ignores it and only the tip-only peel could be defeated by it - still owes no round and still merges. THE SECOND DISPOSABLE CLASS, the machinery's own MECHANICAL adjudication close admitted by mechanical_close_attestation, is driven beside it in the same idiom - the positive and its subject/path refusals - so the peel reads as a verified ADMISSION and not as a subject match. The positive: a mechanical close written through the composed close subject and touching only docs/work/ is asserted to REALLY have moved the branch's tree - without which the test would pass on a peel that had nothing to do - and the round it follows still governs and still merges, with no legacy rollup present anywhere; without that peel the close archiving a judged row stales the APPROVE that had just judged it, which is the failure this arm exists for and the one an adjudication lane cannot avoid by ordering, since its round is drawn while the row is still in active/. The two peels are then driven COMPOSING, a station refresh stacked on the close, because a lane produces them in that order. The refusals, and every one of them is driven with the OTHER clauses satisfied, so each is the single thing that turns its commit away. A close carrying a HAND-WRITTEN subject is an ordinary work commit and does not peel; a commit with the PUBLIC mechanical prefix/suffix but a FORGED middle is refused because the attestor derives the actual active/ -> complete/ WI ids from the no-renames git diff and re-composes their exact canonical subject; a close carrying the machinery's own subject that also touched a path OUTSIDE docs/work/ does not peel either; and INSIDE docs/work/ is not enough, because only the move itself may create or destroy - a close that SMUGGLED a brand-new spec in beside the move, and a close that DESTROYED an already-terminal archived record beside it, are each refused, since peeling either would measure a spec's injection or a judged row's deletion at the parent where no reviewer ever saw it. A close whose pairs came out of a SECOND lane's active/ directory is refused by the one-source-branch requirement, driven with everything else valid - paths confined, deletions paired with their own additions, the subject exactly the one the writer composes for those ids - so nothing but that clause can be answering. THE MULTI-ROW SHAPE is driven too: a close moving two rows does not peel, under either historical joined or current one-item subject; empty and multi-row shapes decline toward more review, and one deletion implies one source branch. All the refusal arms are asserted to leave the gate refusing BY NAME on the round no longer naming the current tree, which is the fail-toward-MORE-review direction every unverified identity-moving step here takes. THE WRITER IS DRIVEN AGAINST THE VERIFIER, not only against fixtures the test file composes itself: a REAL close is landed through handback.close_adjudication and the commit it produces is asserted to peel back to exactly the rev the lane was on, so an ordering or a spelling that drifted on either side is a red rather than a silently un-peelable close on every adjudication lane. THE EMPTY CLOSE is driven where it is OBSERVABLE and its consequence is stated rather than assumed to match the others: a commit carrying the composed subject and a single parent that changed NOTHING - a real --allow-empty commit, since a zero-path diff is the one close shape a fixture cannot reach by writing files - is asserted refused AT mechanical_close_attestation, and deliberately NOT asserted at the gate, because measurement says the gate cannot see this refusal at all. Its refusal is OVER-DETERMINED and no clause owns it, which is stated rather than glossed: the one-source-branch requirement turns it away first, and with THAT deleted the empty diff derives no ids at all, whose composed subject (`adjudicate:  -> complete/ (mechanical close)`) cannot equal the one the commit carries - so the exact-subject comparison refuses it regardless, and there is deliberately no third non-emptiness clause, which could only ever fire where these two already had. The consequence is asserted beside the refusal because they are the honest pair: an empty commit preserves the identity by construction, so governing_rev's walk-through step reaches the real close underneath either way, and a test asserting a gate refusal here would be asserting a behaviour the module does not have and should not, since a commit that changed nothing has invalidated no verdict. THE TWO PEELS' REFUSAL ARMS are held by tests/test_integrate_station.py, cited beside this module because integrate re-exports these very functions (refresh_attestation, work_tip) and the station suite is where a refresh can be produced rather than hand-written: a genuine refresh attested to the sha it produced; a forged Bar-Green trailer in three shapes, the sharpest being a genuine refresh message copied verbatim onto another commit; an amend that keeps the message while the tree moves, revoking the attestation; the deliberately forged attestation recorded as a STATED limit rather than a defence; and the reset peel's data-loss half - an honest work commit merely QUOTING the trailer is never peeled away, and a genuine refresh above it peels back to exactly that commit. BOTH carriers are driven, not only the convenient one: that non-empty telemetry commit, and then the EMPTY commit agent_common.commit_telemetry writes when a Review-Verdict attestation must land on unchanged bookkeeping - obtained by CALLING that producer rather than by hand, so the two cannot drift apart, and asserted to really be zero-path, because that is the commit shape a walk classifying PATHS could not classify and so stopped at, burying the refresh under the very commit that recorded the approval. A WORK commit above the refresh does re-owe and does refuse, so the walk is proven to step through what cannot invalidate a verdict rather than through everything. BOTH ORDERS of refresh and round, because only one of them was covered and the other was broken: the round drawn AFTER the refresh - the order the shipped path actually produces, since a lane's refresh is spawned as soon as its worker is DONE and before the merge slot runs, so any slot refusal parks a branch with a refresh and no round - cites the POST-refresh sha, asserted in the fixture to be that sha and not the pre-refresh one, and is asserted to serve the lane at both readers and to carry the coordinator's attestation under the key the cross-check looks it up by, while a rework above it still re-owes. THE ATTESTATION'S CARRIER IS SCOPED TO ITS OWN PATHS, on BOTH arms and not only the one that carries a pathspec: with an unrelated work file staged and the bookkeeping unchanged, the commit agent_common.commit_telemetry writes for NAMED paths and the one it writes for NO paths at all - the call this suite itself makes, and the arm where a scope appended only when paths exist evaporates - are each asserted zero-path with the caller's index left exactly as found, so work cannot land under a bookkeeping label nor an attestation ride a commit that changed the tree. THE DIAL: the three values over a brief-and-drafts matrix, an unrecognized value falling to when-minting rather than to never, and an adjudication lane closing with a successor draft merging with no verdict artifact of any kind under both never and when-minting, while a spine draft still owes its round. THE DIAL AT THE SCHEDULER, the half a reader could otherwise only take on trust: a committing ADJUDICATE session is driven through the loop's own bookkeeping arm on a closed-lane repository at every dial value - including the `always` no repository fixture had reached - and the review queue it leaves is asserted together with the train-scoped diff range and the recorded judging family, which is what \"exactly as a committing BUILD does\" has to mean. Its INPUT is driven beside it: a branch carrying its spec in BOTH homes, the terminal copy drafting a spine successor and a stale active copy an ordinary one, is asserted to answer the scheduler and the merge gate the SAME way, with the shared precedence also driven pure on a two-path list and on the empty one. THE SHARED DEFINITION, in BOTH its dimensions. WHICH TREE: the C2 review-owed derivation answers owed after a rework and served after a fresh round, and record-only commits after the verdict re-owe nothing. HOW MANY PHASES: at a declared policy of 2 a lone logged REVIEW-A APPROVE is REFUSED by name and the gate clears only once a governing REVIEW-B joins it at the same identity; and the half-drawn round a killed run leaves - REVIEW-A served, the in-memory phase queue gone - is answered by both readers together, the derivation naming REVIEW-B and ONLY REVIEW-B while the gate refuses, then both agreeing once it lands, with the same fixture asserted SERVED at policy 1 so the answer is proven to come from the declared count. The phase span is driven pure at the values neither caller reaches - a negative policy, which a bare slice would answer by slicing from the END, and an over-dialled one - and an unparseable or refusable round is owed on both sides: it is drawn again and never clears the gate. The one class the readers still disagree on is a dissent: it is served for `phases_owed` and refused by the gate. THE TIER IS THE WHOLE CITED SET'S, not the majority's: the cited set includes slow modules, including test_integrate_admission, test_integrate_station, test_handback, test_bar_attestation and test_verdict_record, so Full is the cheapest tier at which EVERY arm above actually runs and Smoke would have claimed commit-floor coverage for a set the commit floor only partly runs. Tier and the pytest marker remain independent declarations that no check compares (registry-machinery-reference �12.2); this cell is labelled on the side that under-claims. THE GATING-SCOPE AND FILING BOUNDARY: a coordinator-recorded final claim-base round clears only with persisted-final-reviewer mode and reviewer retention on; retained-session full rounds and narrow rounds hold; a missing claim base holds by name; the full claim-base range survives a trunk refresh while a partial range cannot gate; a partial or refusable latest round holds without falling back to an older APPROVE and is owed again; neither a narrow approve nor an invalid round suppresses the unchanged-rework page; and a legacy rollup never clears. THE BAR ATTESTATION: a trailer validates only when its column-0 single label has its own tree and first parent, a known bar, and a tests digest; wrong tree or parent, missing or unknown bar, missing tests, a quoted or duplicate label refuse. Digesting normalizes and de-duplicates named paths, is order-independent, differs for a changed set, and gives none for an empty set. A verified review attestation is never recognized as a refresh by work_tip or governing_rev, while the read-only walk still steps through an identity-preserving review carrier; verified landing and no-bar refresh attestations still peel. The refresh writes landing or no-bar through the shared producer, and refresh and attest both reach that producer.\"\"\"\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
